      "message": "Probably ok, I guess the ipv6 name here is the same as L.1339. \n\nL.1339 gets {ipv4, ipv6} interface names (if any) which are sent by Tethering class. Tethering class get the ipv6 interface names by TetheringInterfaceUtils::getTetheringInterfaces::getIPv6Interface which parsing UpstreamNetworkState object\n\nNeed to discuss with mark to confirm\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base.git/+/fc2b39948c607cfa723f72c1ab965ad50d0419d2/packages/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/TetheringInterfaceUtils.java#49\npublic static @Nullable InterfaceSet getTetheringInterfaces(UpstreamNetworkState ns) {\n        final String if4 \u003d getInterfaceForDestination(lp, INADDR_ANY);\n        final String if6 \u003d getIPv6Interface(ns);\n\n        return (if4 \u003d\u003d null \u0026\u0026 if6 \u003d\u003d null) ? null : new InterfaceSet(if4, if6);\n}\n    /**\n     * Get the upstream interface for IPv6 tethering.\n     * @return null if there is no usable interface, or the interface name otherwise.\n     */\n    public static @Nullable String getIPv6Interface(UpstreamNetworkState ns) {",
