      "message": "It looks like we are deleting the code that populates the map for IPv6 upstream interfaces.\n\nIn the case where the IPv6 upstream interface is different from the IPv4 interface (e.g., rmnet_data0 vs. v4-rmnet_data0), will the IPv6-only interface be in the map? Will line 1341 have run on \"rmnet_data0\"? Or will it only have run on \"v4-rmnet_data0\"?\n\nThere may be unit tests that you can use to test this assumption. I don\u0027t think there is anything in IpServerTest, because the upstream interface selection code is not there. Perhaps this is, or could be, covered by a unit test in TetheringTest?\n\nOr, we could test this on a real device on T-Mobile. Temporarily hack TetheringConfiguration#checkDunRequired to always return false and see what happens.",
