      "writtenOn": "2021-04-02T03:49:52Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "For a 464xlat network, IPv4 can appear up after IPv6. For a dual-stack network, I think IPv6 always appears after IPv6 because Tethering sends CMD_TETHER_CONNECTION_CHANGED first before calling IPv6TetheringCoordinator#updateUpstreamNetworkState.\n\nSetting this in two places SGTM for now. I think the right thing to do is to just have BpfCoordinator deal with interface names and maintain an authoritative map between names and indices. But for that to happen I think we\u0027d have to move some of the IPv6 rule addition code from IpServer to BpfCoordinator.",
